# -*- mode: org -*-
#+TITLE: The queue for rcc
#+STARTUP: overview
#+OPTIONS: toc:nil ^:nil
#+TODO: TODO WAITING | DONE

The queue, one chapter per part of the tree, in the order the work is
wanted; within a chapter, priority order top first. Each entry states
the fact, the fix and the check that settles it. A =WAITING= entry is
investigated and reported and waits on its owner; it leaves when the
fix it waits for lands and its check passes. Finished entries leave;
git keeps them.

#+TOC: headlines 2

* Guarantees

The promises in =docs/guarantees.md=, draft 1. The entries are the
decisions the draft marks, the measurements that inform them, and one
verification. The entry number is the guarantee it belongs to. G4, G5,
G8 and G11 are decided: the target's division instruction, =freeze=
with no value of the compiler's own, the integer round trip for
pointer arithmetic, and align what you can prove.

** TODO G8: price the round trip

All three tiers of G8 are promised; the pointer add is the integer
round trip wherever the front end cannot prove the arithmetic stays
inside a declared object. The cost to alias analysis and loop
vectorization is the project's first published number, not a vote
on the promise. Needs code.

Fix: measure once the front end emits pointer arithmetic.

Check: the corpus compiled with the round trip everywhere, then with
"gep what you can prove", and what the vectorizer and alias analysis
still do in each.

** TODO G13: left-to-right evaluation stays

Left-to-right evaluation departs from K&R, who left the order open so
the compiler could choose the cheaper one. The draft includes it as
the one promise ISO withholds that costs nothing with LLVM behind.

Fix: confirm the promise stays.

Check: the argument order costs nothing beyond a register move on
x86-64 and aarch64.

** TODO Calls through a mismatched function type

Left out of the list as not deliverable past the ABI: the call goes
out per the pointer's type, and =instcombine= rewrites a direct call
through a cast when it thinks it safe.

Fix: decide whether a partial promise, indirect calls only, is worth
writing.

Check: what =instcombine= does to a direct call through a cast.

